       "prompt": "Show that $f(x)=x^3-4x$ is an odd function, and hence evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-2}^{2}(x^3-4x)\\,dx$.",
       "answer": {
        "short": "$f(-x)=-f(x)$, so $f$ is odd; the integral is $0$.",
        "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)^3-4(-x)\\\\&=-x^3+4x\\\\&=-f(x)\\end{align*}$$\nSo $f$ is odd. The limits $-2$ and $2$ are symmetric, so the areas above and below the axis cancel:\n$$\\int_{-2}^{2}(x^3-4x)\\,dx=0.$$"
       },
