     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p50-theory",
     "replacement": "On an interval where $[f(x)]^n$ is defined, the reverse chain rule applies when the integrand contains the derivative of the inner function, allowing for a constant factor.\n\n$$\\int f'(x)[f(x)]^n\\,dx=\\frac{[f(x)]^{n+1}}{n+1}+C,\\qquad n\\ne-1$$\n\n1. Identify the inner function $f(x)$.\n2. Check whether the expression contains $f'(x)$ or a constant multiple of it.\n  If it does not, you cannot use this rule.\n3. Adjust for any missing constant factors.\n4. Write the result as $\\frac{[f(x)]^{n+1}}{n+1}+C$, including the constant adjustment from step 3.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p50-theory",
     "targetFingerprint": "64b20f9cfd628f0135623b0196157a5d72e9c41660cc13100bb9a5f7fef29f2f",
